Derivative notes
----------------

The fork is based on pixelmatch v8.0.0, commit ab76f52 ("cleanup readme"). Its git history is
preserved: the upstream commits are present in this repository, and the changes made here are
isolated in commits on top of them. To list them:

    git log --oneline upstream/main..HEAD

Files that carry upstream code unchanged:
    index.js            (for the same behaviour; extended, see below)
    bin/pixelmatch      (unmodified upstream CLI)
    test/fixtures/*     (unmodified upstream fixtures)
    test/test.js        (unmodified upstream test suite)

Files added by this fork:
    triage.js                       rich comparison API
    triage.d.ts                     its type declarations
    lib/regions.js                  connected-component regions
    lib/shift.js                    global shift estimation and compensation
    lib/annotate.js                 region boxes and bitmap labels on a diff image
    bin/pixelmatch-triage.js        CLI that reports regions, JSON and annotated PNG
    test/triage.js                  tests for the added behaviour
    bench/triage-bench.js           measurement harness for the added cost
    examples/scenario.mjs           reproduction of the motivating problem

Modifications to upstream code in index.js are additive and opt-in:
    - new optional `detailMask` and `detailDeltas` options
    - identical-input fast path also resets those two caller-provided buffers
    - new internal helper `hyabMagnitude`, used only when `detailDeltas` is requested
The default call path, its return value and its error messages are unchanged; the upstream test
suite runs unmodified and passes.

What is NOT inherited
---------------------

No code, data, or assets were taken from any other project. The region clustering, shift
estimation, annotation renderer and CLI in this repository were written for this fork. They do not
copy from popular implementations of the same ideas; the algorithms are implemented from their
published descriptions or from first principles, as noted in the source comments.
